  │
  ▼
Forward traffic
________________________________________
26. But there is a deeper issue
Suppose:
Backend A → healthy
Backend B → healthy
Backend C → healthy
Health check says:
✓ ✓ ✓
But:
A → 10ms latency
B → 10ms latency
C → 2 seconds latency
All are technically healthy.
Yet C is struggling.
A basic health check doesn't necessarily capture this.
This leads us toward:
latency-aware routing
load-aware routing
adaptive load balancing
Modern infrastructure can become much more sophisticated than simple Round Robin.
________________________________________
27. The real objective
The objective isn't:
"Give every server exactly the same number of requests."
The real objective is closer to:
Distribute work so that the overall system remains healthy, efficient, and low-latency.
That distinction is extremely important.
Think:
                Goal
                 │
        ┌────────┼────────┐
        ▼        ▼        ▼
     latency  throughput  stability
        │        │        │
        └────────┼────────┘
                 ▼
